# Whitelist approach: ignore EVERYTHING, then re-include only the files we want in the repo.
# This keeps PyCharm's generated files (.idea/), caches (__pycache__/, apicache/), the
# HelpersPackage/Log/PDFHelpers symlinks, user-password.py, and any future junk out of git
# automatically -- so PyCharm's Commit no longer offers them.
#
# To track a new file, add another "!name" line for it below.
*
!.gitignore
!FancyDownloader.py
!user-config.py
!FancyDownloader.ico
